    "mapping_notes": [
      "Complete publisher-edition poem (PTS/BJTS), not a line-complete translation of every VRI stanza. Whole-poem correspondence does not imply segment, line or word equivalence. Preserve independent VRI wording, variant notes and edition differences; do not invent missing words or transfer another poem’s refrain.",
      "Publisher main PTS heading409, BJTS brace/file412 and canonical tha-ap414 are distinct verified identities. The Candabhāgā hermitage, Atthadassi encounter, single umbrella offering, prediction and named Ekachattiya colophons establish this particular correspondence.",
      "All47 four-line stanzas and85 original notes remain complete publisher-edition scope. Preserve attributed botanical/fish identifications, lexical alternatives and PTS/BJTS readings without modernization or canonical harmonization. Eleven source-owned display occurrences retain exact case and doubled-letter forms.",
      "Notes10/57/75 retain original unfinished or mismatched punctuation, including note57’s unclosed parenthesis. Keep every published word; neither an intended completion nor closing punctuation is supplied. No chapter apparatus is assigned. Full publisher final refrains do not expand the three independent VRI peyyāla stanzas."
    ],
